  nonce: b6db  # b6db
  message: "Batch 5a (java, kotlin, php) measured this gap. Kotlin: the analyzer's run-wide Type.m lookup is gone and typed calls go through the linker's method index, which keeps the last overload: 255 edges on okhttp and detekt-core keep their qualified name and change overload. A blind judge read 15 retargeted Kotlin edges: 9 wrong before and right now, 2 wrong both times, 3 RIGHT BEFORE AND WRONG NOW, all three overloads the argument count decides (server.start() now on the private start(InetSocketAddress); server.takeRequest() now on takeRequest(timeout, unit)); also wrong among gained edges: url(HttpUrl) on url(URL), addHeader(String) on addHeader(name, value). Java: 2 of 10 sampled binds through a static import are toByteArray(long) bound to toByteArray(boolean). java.py now selects among a class's OWN overloads by argument count in the analyzer (352 retargeted, 15 of 15 sampled wrong before and right now), which the shared layer does not do. Proposal: the argument count as a stub fact, the method index keeping every overload, selection by count (defaults and varargs read from the declaration), before batch 5b moves more languages onto the index. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/batch5a_11262026/judge/."  # b6db
